# Tester: factory settings for the Bizzybot bridge. Merge these into the box's
# /workspaces/env/agent.env, then restart agent.service. Non-secret:
# REGISTRATION_TOKEN, GH_TOKEN and CLAUDE_CODE_OAUTH_TOKEN arrive via the dropbox,
# and so does TESTER_MAILBOX_PASSWORD, the Google Workspace sign-in password for the
# shared mailbox. It signs Gmail itself in so the traveler's magic-link mail can be
# read; no app login uses it. 2-Step Verification is off on that account so the agent
# can sign itself in, and Google issues no app password for an account without it.
CLAUDE_CWD=/workspaces/projects/btdash
CLAUDE_MODEL=opus
# The browsers are two chrome-devtools MCP servers, one per account
# (TESTER_*_PROFILE below).
CLAUDE_CHROME=0
CLAUDE_PERMISSION_MODE=bypassPermissions
# Role protocol, appended to every session's system prompt (read at session start).
AGENT_PROMPT_FILE=/workspaces/projects/cloud-agents/factory/tester/PROTOCOL.md
# Slack user ids of the agents allowed to wake this one with a mention (BzPM).
AGENT_MENTIONS_FROM=<Uxxxx>
# Stop a chain of agent-to-agent turns after this many.
AGENT_CHAIN_LIMIT=25
# The operator account: superadmin, owns the shared mailbox.
# It configures orgs and reads admin pages. It never books. It signs in with Google
# SSO: a superadmin is never emailed a sign-in link, however the page answers.
TESTER_OPERATOR_EMAIL=tester@biztrip.ai
# The traveler account: role "user", books everything. Signs in by magic link — the
# only account of the two that can, and the credentials provider gates roles, so
# neither account has a password here.
# A plus-address on the operator's mailbox, so its mail arrives there too.
TESTER_TRAVELER_EMAIL=tester+2@biztrip.ai
# The shared mailbox the traveler's magic-link mail lands in — the operator's own
# address, so check every mail's To: line. Read in Gmail from the operator's
# browser, not over IMAP.
TESTER_MAILBOX_EMAIL=tester@biztrip.ai
# Chrome user data directories, one per account, passed as --userDataDir
# to that account's chrome-devtools MCP server — chrome-devtools-operator
# and chrome-devtools-traveler, registered at user scope and run --headless.
# They persist, so the Gmail and BizTrip sessions live here between runs:
# neither server takes --isolated, and one directory serves one browser at
# a time.
TESTER_OPERATOR_PROFILE=/workspaces/chrome/tester-operator
TESTER_TRAVELER_PROFILE=/workspaces/chrome/tester-traveler
